{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794228995,"nonce":"iC28/wE58qKBv9ANMvl2xvhHuEE=","title":"RCWA interior field is silently NaN when an order sits at grazing incidence","message":"With a period of exactly two wavelengths in air, the (+-2,0) and (0,+-2) orders have kz = 0 in the air layer. field3d() / field() then return NaN in every layer above that one (stack_amplitudes_interior gives NaN amplitudes), while efficiency('R') and efficiency('T') stay finite, so nothing signals the problem. Reproduction: a three-layer stack (quartz 0.5 | patterned 0.36 | air 0.5), period (2, 2), wavelength 1, orders 25: 52 of 82 z-slices of field3d() are NaN; orders 9 (which drops those orders) or a period of 2.1 give none. Expected: a clear error naming the grazing order (or a regularised amplitude), not NaN.","files":null}]}